hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, that Malik narrated to him, on the authority of Suhail ibn Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When a Muslim or believing servant performs ablution and washes his face, she comes out of He faces every sin he saw with his eyes along with the water or with the last drop of water. When he washes his hands, every sin from his hands comes out. His hands splashed it with water or with the last drop of water, so when he washed his feet, every sin that he committed with his feet with water or with water is removed. The last drop of water until it comes out clean of sins.”"
